## Actions, in order

**1. Bash, foreground** (read-only, takes seconds)

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
WT=~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive
herdr agent list                                    # wgka, adv-codex, adv-fable: idle, focused=false
herdr agent read wgka --source visible --lines 30   # context left
git -C $WT rev-parse --short HEAD; git -C $WT status --short
grep -n -i 'timeout' $WT/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-27-ccs-wg-keepalive-relay-design.md
grep -rn 'proxy_read_timeout' $WT/projects/ccs/roles/host_proxy/
ls ~/work/ccs.ansible/orchestrator/quorum/ | tail -3
```

The ballot goes out only if the spec fixes no value; if it does, that value is already decided and I relay it instead.

**2. Write** `orchestrator/quorum/ballot-17.md` (B16 is the last id I know of; step 1 confirms):

```
Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box. Rules: quorum/protocol.md.

B17 — Upstream read timeout of the WireGuard keepalive relay location
  Context:
  - Worktree .claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive, branch feat/wg-keepalive-relay, HEAD <sha, step 1>.
    Plan step 6 of 11; steps 7-11 build on it.
  - The location relays PUT /key/wg/<org>/<user>/<server> to http://127.0.0.1:9700.
  - The spec sets no read timeout (grep, step 1).
  - proxy_read_timeout values already in roles/host_proxy: <grep output, step 1>.
  - Not measured: Pritunl's response time for this PUT; the client's own request timeout.
  - The options differ only when the upstream takes longer than 5 s to answer.
  a) proxy_read_timeout 5s in the relay location.
     Upstream silent: the request ends with 504 and frees its connection after 5 s.
     Upstream answering in 5-60 s: the keepalive fails.
     One more directive to render and pin in tests.
     Cost if wrong: keepalives fail while Pritunl is slow but alive.
     Rollback: one-line template change, re-run playbook 55 on the gateway.
  b) No directive; nginx default 60 s.
     Upstream silent: each request holds its connection for up to 60 s.
     Upstream answering in 5-60 s: the answer is relayed.
     No new directive.
     Cost if wrong: connections to a hung upstream accumulate.
     Rollback: the same one-line change and run.
Reply one line:  B17: <letter> — <rationale>     (or  B17: X: <proposal>)
```

**3. Bash, three background calls in one message** (`run_in_background: true`)

```bash
herdr agent prompt adv-codex "$(cat orchestrator/quorum/ballot-17.md)" --wait --timeout 900000; \
herdr agent read adv-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > orchestrator/inbox/adv-codex.last
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt adv-fable "$(cat orchestrator/quorum/ballot-17.md)" --wait --timeout 900000; \
herdr agent read adv-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > orchestrator/inbox/adv-fable.last
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt wgka "$(cat orchestrator/scratch/park-wgka-b17.txt)" --wait --timeout 300000; \
herdr agent read wgka --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > orchestrator/inbox/wgka.last
```

`park-wgka-b17.txt` reads:

> Ballot B17 is open on the step-6 read timeout. Two voting advisors decide it and I relay the result. Your recommendation is recorded as a proposal, not a decision. Until then, do not write step 6 and do not start steps 7-11: no provisional value, and no variable or default standing in for the choice. Commit finished work locally, then stop and report: phase, branch, head SHA, `git status --short`, next step. Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box.

If step 1 shows `wgka` at 50% context used or more, its park report is followed by a background `/compact mid-task: keep the brief, the decisions, DIR/branch/head SHA and the open items`.

**4. Backlog.** Edit the task's row in `orchestrator/backlog.md`: next step "step 6 after B17", blocked-on "B17 (vote)", decisions "+B17 open". Then run `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh` in the foreground and republish the Artifact at the same page.

**5. Status to the operator** (no poll):

> **Now:** the executor stopped at step 6 of 11 on one choice: how long the relay waits for Pritunl's answer before giving up (5 s or nginx's default 60 s). That is ballot B17, now with both voting advisors. Nothing that depends on it is being built. Nothing has changed on live machines.
>
> **Next:** on 2/2 I relay the decision and steps 6-11 continue. Then come the Codex review at the exact SHA, my own validation run, the merge vote, the canary-go vote and the deploy to ccs-it from merged main. None of that needs you. I cannot yet say whether it lands tonight. A split on B17 would wait for you as a poll.
>
> **You:** nothing now. Acceptance is yours: once you see my "canary live on ccs-it" status, connect with your own WireGuard profile for ccs-it, run `ping -i 0.2 172.27.96.2` for 3 minutes, and paste the closing summary lines (sent/received, loss, round-trip). The fleet rollout does not start before that.
>
> **Not verified:** the executor's claim that Pritunl answers in milliseconds; it has not been measured.
>
> Backlog: claude.ai/artifact/Pr6sWRSgfJ76QjjFo5erEJ

This status is in English because this session's language setting requires it; the standing ruling asks for Russian.

**6. On each notification:** read the `.last` file, then `herdr agent get <name>`, and write `quorum/ballot-17.results.md`. A 2/2 result goes to `wgka` as `DECIDED B17` in a background prompt with a time box.

## Why

- **The choice is the vote's.** A choice between alternatives that changes the outcome is not mine to make, and it is not one of the operator's four kinds of decision. "No trivia" and the manifest agree: a 2/2 result is reported, not asked.
- **The ballot is neutral.** The executor's recommendation and its two supporting claims are stripped. "Matches every other location" is replaced by the grep output, because `CLAUDE.md` records 3600 s on the WebSocket locations. The response-time claim is listed as unmeasured.
- **The executor parks.** Steps 7-11 all build on step 6, so there is no independent work. A provisional 5 s would be rework if it loses, and would tilt the vote toward what already exists.
- **"Canary tonight" approves nothing.** It is a wish about timing, so every gate still runs in order at the exact SHA. I promise no time I cannot verify.
- **Acceptance is an instruction.** It needs the operator's own profile and hands, and hard rule #17 forbids me the end-user path. It is written now, so it costs them nothing until they are back.
- **Background waiters.** Both advisors get the ballot at once so neither sees the other's vote, and I stay free to supervise.
